## Scope discipline

CX-4 is **not** a lower bound on every encoding. It only rules out coordinate-blind states invariant under row-assignment permutations / unordered row-profile multisets. Likewise, CX-1 does not show that every class has a one-bit state; it shows that identifiability depth cannot be reinterpreted as a storage lower bound without an additional representation/access theorem.
